leios.theme.grub-theme (1.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Enable the theme through defaults instead of editing /etc/default/grub:
    - ship /etc/default/grub.d/leios-theme.cfg, which sets GRUB_THEME and
      GRUB_GFXMODE only if they are not set in /etc/default/grub;
    - provide the background through the desktop-grub alternative used by
      /etc/grub.d/05_debian_theme, so GRUB_BACKGROUND or an image in
      /boot/grub/ still take precedence.
  * On upgrade, remove the "# LeiOS GRUB theme" block (GRUB_THEME,
    GRUB_BACKGROUND and GRUB_GFXMODE) that earlier versions appended to
    /etc/default/grub.
  * Only run update-grub when GRUB has been set up and not in containers,
    like /etc/kernel/postinst.d/zz-update-grub.

 -- Linus Fischer <leicraft@leicraftmc.de>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0100

leios.theme.grub-theme (1.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

